content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-105, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22000, on the filtered-water line. P-105 is within the P-101 to P-106 group whose lines are chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite. [C01, C13, C16]",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage: the applicable manual symptom is 'Leakage at shaft seal'. Its documented corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. No numerical allowable leak rate or leak-based shutdown limit is provided.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.9 mm/s: applying the HF-300 Figure 3 bearing-housing vibration-velocity scale in mm/s RMS, this is within Zone B, 2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is below the 4.5 mm/s RMS Zone C boundary and the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone D boundary; it does not meet the site rule for vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature 71 C: the applicable manual limits are for temperature measured on the bearing-housing surface. Normal is up to 70 C, alarm is 80 C, and trip is 90 C. The reading is therefore 1 C above normal, 9 C below alarm, and 19 C below trip. It is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, so the SSP-07 requirement to raise a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Immediate-stop and priority screen: neither the vibration-reading stop criterion nor the temperature-alarm P1 criterion is met by the supplied readings, so stop_equipment_now is false and P1 is not automatically required. Corrective seal work is still required. P2 is a provisional planning selection because the evidence does not define P2/P3 response criteria.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal failure from worn or cracked seal faces, previous dry running, or shaft misalignment; these are the manual-listed causes of leakage at the shaft seal, and the report does not distinguish between them.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the installed seal is HF3-450, early failure associated with the revised sleeve tolerance is a documented failure mode for this pump's serial range. The bulletin specifically covers serial HF3-22000 and above, but the installed seal type is not reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the above-normal housing temperature, investigate over-greasing, bearing wear, and misalignment. Bearing replacement is not established merely by the 71 C reading; the troubleshooting table calls for grease-quantity and alignment checks and bearing replacement if worn.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment, bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation are documented vibration-related causes to inspect during troubleshooting, although the reported 3.9 mm/s value itself classifies as Zone B rather than a restricted or damage-likely zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before starting seal work, electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC. Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, drain and vent the pump, and obtain the required line-break permit before breaking into the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves throughout the work because P-105 is on a sodium-hypochlorite-dosed filtered-water line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before removing the back pull-out assembly, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. The assembly mass is 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg threshold for these controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "With the pump isolated and drained, remove the back pull-out assembly. The back pull-out design permits removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework. Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the existing seal and sleeve.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the withdrawn sleeve for scoring. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth; otherwise the evidence does not require sleeve replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the accompanying conditions before reassembly: check alignment, inspect the bearings and impeller, check NPSH, and check bearing grease quantity. If bearing inspection establishes wear requiring replacement, replace both bearings as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new HF3-450B cartridge mechanical seal and one new casing gasket. Do not fit HF3-450 on this pump. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting; this does not remove the separate requirement to inspect the sleeve for scoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten all disturbed fasteners. For Table 5 fasteners with lightly oiled threads, tighten the M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, and any disturbed M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm. Tighten the seal gland nuts for HF3-450B to 30 Nm under SB-2026-014, not the superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Carry out the troubleshooting alignment check using a laser alignment tool, and always repeat laser alignment after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before operating the pump, confirm the Plan 11 seal-flush arrangement from pump discharge is in service. Never run the seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "At close-out, record the seal-leak check, bearing-housing surface temperature, and vibration-velocity readings from both bearing housings. Resume weekly two-housing vibration monitoring and classify the highest reading with Figure 3. Zone C requires restricted operation with maintenance planned; Zone D requires immediate shutdown and notification of the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; required replacement for HF3-450 on this serial range. Quantity one.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "NOT SPECIFIED IN EVIDENCE",
      "description": "New casing gasket required during mechanical-seal replacement; obtain the correct part number before assembly.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft sleeve: supply one only if inspection shows scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth; otherwise no replacement sleeve is required by the evidence.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC are mandatory for work inside the pump or on its seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate both suction and discharge valves and use a line-break permit, draining and venting before the line is broken.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because the task is on a chemically dosed line containing sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; the manual also expressly requires lifting equipment for this assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Base mechanical-seal replacement allowance: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-alignment allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional allowance only if inspection establishes that the bearings must be replaced: bearing-pair replacement is 6.0 hours with 2 technicians; it is not included in the base seal-replacement scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection and gland torque: manual section 5.2 directs tightening to Table 5, and Table 5 lists 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, applies to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above, which expressly includes this asset at the boundary serial. The service bulletin therefore governs the seal-specific requirements: do not fit HF3-450; use HF3-450B and 30 Nm gland torque. Table 5 remains applicable to the other listed fasteners. The below-serial provision allowing HF3-450 and the old table does not apply to P-105.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve-measurement wording: the bulletin says the pre-set HF3-450B needs no sleeve measurement, while the manual requires the withdrawn sleeve to be inspected for scoring. Apply these to different purposes: omit sleeve measurement for setting the pre-set seal, but retain the scoring inspection and replace HF3-455 when scoring exceeds the bulletin's 0.1 mm depth criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Confirm that the reported 3.9 mm/s vibration value is RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, identify its measurement location, and provide the other housing reading. The manual requires classification of the highest reading from both housings (C06, C07).",
    "Identify the seal currently installed and whether it is HF3-450; the bulletin failure mode is conditional on that component being fitted, and the report does not identify it (C13).",
    "Obtain the casing-gasket part number. The manual requires a new casing gasket but the supplied evidence does not identify its part number (C10).",
    "Record the sleeve scoring result during disassembly so the conditional requirement for HF3-455 can be decided without guesswork (C10, C13).",
    "The evidence does not provide alignment results, grease quantity, bearing condition, impeller condition, NPSH findings, or dry-run/flush history. These inspections are needed to establish root cause and whether any additional parts or bearing-pair labour are required (C02, C09, C10).",
    "The evidence does not quantify the leak or provide a leak-rate-based operating/shutdown criterion. Operations should confirm whether the actual leakage requires action sooner than this provisional P2 plan; stop_equipment_now=false is based on the supplied vibration and temperature criteria, not on an assessed leak rate (C07, C09, C15).",
    "SSP-07 defines the temperature-related P1 trigger but does not define P2/P3 response times or scheduling rules. Confirm the provisional P2 assignment and required completion date with site planning (C15)."
  ]
}
